      "observed": "HouseruleMechanics.initialize (orphan) was the only installer of house-rule hooks (feat grants on setting change/createActor, recovery on rest, status effects on updateActor, flanking, skill training, healing integration, block, condition track, grapple). Current settings are read by live rule modules (CombatRules, SkillRules, ForceRules, ConditionTrackRules read flankingEnabled, criticalHitVariant, deathSystem, feintSkill, blockMechanicalAlternative, conditionTrackCap), and the GM UI is GMHouseRulesSurfaceService, so the orphan cluster appears superseded. Whether every exposed setting has a live effect was not traced (suspected per rule). houserule-grapple is test-only.",
      "intendedOwnership": "Each exposed house rule has exactly one live implementation in its owning rule module.",
      "contractRef": "A-09; R-HRL-03",
      "proposedSolution": "Build a per-setting table (setting key -> live reader module) from the manifest; delete the orphan cluster (legacy C) for settings with a live reader; list settings with no live reader as UNIMPLEMENTED for the owner (do not silently drop or invent behaviour).",
      "alternatives": "",
      "dependencies": [
        "combat/skills/force contracts"
      ],
      "ownerDecisionRequired": true,
      "rulesQuestion": false,
      "regressionTests": "Census test: every manifest key has >=1 live reader outside houserules/ and ui.",
      "foundryAcceptance": "Toggle-to-effect checks per rule.",
      "scope": "M",
      "simplificationBenefit": "~2.6k SLOC removed; clear house-rule ownership.",
      "risk": "Medium: some toggles may currently do nothing.",
      "perfImpact": "none"
    },
